	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Un'Goro Crater is a vast green bowl sunk deep into the south of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, walled by cliffs between the sands of {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link} and the blighted wastes of {link:silithus}Silithus{/link}. Beneath its rim the world seems to belong to another age. Steam rises from its springs, a volcano smokes at its heart, and the jungle is ruled by beasts that the rest of the world has long forgotten: thunderous devilsaurs, stegodons, winged pterrordax and packs of ravasaurs. Strange crystals glitter in the grass, and tall pylons of crystal stand at the edge of the wilds.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how the crater was made, nor when. The histories of the earliest age hold that the servants of the {red:titans}Titans{/red} shaped certain lands of the young world as gardens of wild life, and that Un'Goro was among them. The pylons of crystal that stand around its rim are older than any people now living in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, and none who dwell in the crater today can say who raised them or why. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} who come here to hunt feel the presence of the Earth Mother strongly in the basin. To them its creatures are the nobler kin of the beasts of their own plains.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The crater has lately drawn a crowd of the curious and the stranded. A troupe of explorers led by {link:williden-marshal}Williden Marshal{/link} came to study the land and was nearly destroyed by it. Its survivors hold a rocky refuge on the northern heights, where goblins of {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link}, wandering scholars and lost travellers have gathered around them. The {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} has sent for the crater's soil, which is said to hold potent magic, and druids in {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} and {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} study it. In the south, the insects of the Gorishi hive have dug into the earth. Their presence troubles the scholars, for nothing like them belongs to the crater's natural order. In these days maps also name the {red:shaper-s-terrace}Shaper's Terrace{/red} within the crater, a place whose tale is told on its own page.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The great saurians.{/b} Devilsaurs hunt across the whole basin. Stegodons graze in the south-west, ravasaurs run in packs in the south-east, and diemetradons bask along its paths.
• {b}The apes of {link:fungal-rock}Fungal Rock{/link}.{/b} Great gorillas hold the caves of the north-east and drive off any who come near.
• {b}The Gorishi.{/b} A hive of insects has carved out the {link:the-slithering-scar}Slithering Scar{/link} in the south.
• {b}Elementals.{/b} Beings of living flame walk the slopes of the volcano, and creatures of tar rise from the northern pits.
• {b}Bloodpetals and oozes.{/b} Carnivorous plants creep through the eastern thickets, and slimes gather in the marshes.
• {b}The newcomers.{/b} Explorers, tinkers of {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link} and lost wanderers crowd {link:marshal-s-refuge}Marshal's Refuge{/link}, and a {link:tauren}tauren{/link} hunter keeps his own camp where the road from {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link} enters the crater.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Age of the Makers.{/b} The crater's pylons and crystals remain from a time before any mortal kingdom. No mortal history records their raising.
• {b}The Marshal Expedition.{/b} {link:williden-marshal}Williden Marshal{/link}'s troupe set up camps in the south-west and north-east of the crater. The beasts overran both, and the survivors fled north to higher ground.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Scholars, druids, hunters and at least one wanderer who cannot remember why he came now seek the crater.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Crater",
			text = [=[• At {link:marshal-s-refuge}Marshal's Refuge{/link} it is said that the pylons and the colored crystals in the grass belong together, and that the right mix of colors will wake their power.
• {link:krakle}Krakle{/link} of {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link} believes the springs of {link:golakka-hot-springs}Golakka{/link} draw their heat from the volcano, though his sums are not yet finished.
• {link:torwa-pathfinder}Torwa Pathfinder{/link} warns that {link:lar-korwi}Lar'korwi{/link}, the great ravasaur of the east, will follow for days anyone who steals from his kill.]=],
		},
	},
})

