		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Marshlands are the wet eastern lowlands of the crater, a country of mud, reeds and still water. Slimes of many kinds gather in its pools, and bloodpetals creep through its thickets. One of the expedition's abandoned camps lay on this side of the crater, and its stores sat untouched in the mud long after the explorers fled. A wrecked raft rests beside a small pond further south, far from any water that could have carried it there. It belonged to the wanderer {link:linken}Linken{/link}, though he no longer remembered it.]=],
		},
	},
